** UNSEEN :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
The domain is absent from the map. Not "bad at the subject" — the
subject simply doesn't occupy working attention yet: no vocabulary, no
questions, no recognized boundary. Reserved for mapped, imported, or
inferred nodes not yet consciously examined. Never a birth state for
human-created AIUs; never reviewable (the scheduler cannot test what
has no representation). First contact promotes to AWARE.
** AWARE :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
The domain has become an identified object of possible knowledge: "I
know there is something here that I do not yet know." Questions begin
to exist — the learner can say "I don't understand X" rather than
staring through X. This is the birth state of every human-created
AIU, because the act of capture is itself the awareness gate. Due for
review immediately: the first successful retrieval starts acquisition.
** ACQUIRING :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
The learner is accumulating and retrieving the building blocks:
terminology, facts, procedures, relationships. Retrieval works on
familiar questions; integration hasn't happened yet. Reached
automatically on the first successful review. Exposure alone never
promotes here — only demonstrated retrieval does.
** UNDERSTANDING :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
The bag of pieces has become a model. The learner can explain why,
predict consequences, derive implications, connect concepts, and spot
misconceptions. Test: hand them a novel example and ask them to
explain it with the model. Requires attested evidence — high recall
scores alone never imply this stage (a beautifully memorized
misunderstanding recalls perfectly).
** CAPABLE :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
The model has become usable. Standard problems get solved, procedures
execute, appropriate methods are selected in familiar situations,
common failures get troubleshot — independently. Reproducing textbook
examples doesn't qualify; performance on unfamiliar examples within
familiar problem classes does. Attested.
** PROFICIENT :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
Use is independent, reliable, and efficient across varied situations.
The characteristic shift, after Dreyfus: from "what rule applies?" to
"what kind of situation is this?" Pattern recognition is strong;
genuinely unprecedented situations still resist. Attested on evidence
of reliability + efficiency + independent method selection.
** EXPERT :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
Deep, organized domain representations supporting rapid, reliable
judgment: salient information recognized at a glance, complex problems
solved, subtle errors diagnosed, incomplete information worked with.
Requires evidence of reproducibly superior performance on
representative tasks — never mere review counts or years of exposure.
Expert intuition counts only inside the domain, under valid feedback.
Attested.
** ADAPTIVE :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
The expert's crucial upgrade (Hatano & Inagaki): knowing when the
known solution is wrong and constructing a better one. The adaptive
expert asks "do the assumptions behind the standard method actually
hold here?", reasons from first principles under ambiguity, and treats
anomalies as data about the model rather than noise. Gate: a novel
problem solved for which no memorized procedure was supplied.
Attested.
** GENERATIVE :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
Crossing from using knowledge to generating new structures: methods,
models, explanations, frameworks, hypotheses that did not previously
exist for the learner. The novelty may still be local — a new proof
technique for one problem counts before anyone judges its field-level
worth. Gate: demonstrated, domain-grounded, explainable novelty.
Attested.
** CONTRIBUTING :AIU_CONTEXT_BODY:
Crossing from my knowledge to the field's knowledge: independently
produced, validated work that extends the collective state of the
domain — novel, relevant, defensible, communicated, and additive.
Peer review, deployed method, new dataset, original interpretation:
the form is domain-dependent, the threshold is not. This is the top of
the spine, and it does not mean "finished": domains evolve, frontiers
move, and contribution is participation, not completion. Attested.
